= Application programming interface =

== Overview ==
An '''application programming interface''' (API) is a defined interface through which software components expose operations, data, or services to other software.

APIs can be local library interfaces, operating-system interfaces, language/runtime interfaces, or remote service interfaces. A Web API is only one kind of API.

An API describes how software can interact with a component; a protocol describes rules for communication between participants. The two can overlap in networked systems but are not identical concepts.

== Boundaries ==
* API ≠ Web API only
* API ≠ network protocol necessarily
* interface ≠ implementation

